From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DosboxMultiplatform <dev@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] android: expose synthetic joystick before DOS startup

The Flutter bridge supplies joystick state through JOYSTICK_Move_* and
JOYSTICK_Button. DOS games probe the game port while autoexec is starting,
before the first framebuffer reaches the bridge, so enabling the port from the
frame hook is too late. Android has no SDL hardware joystick to enable it.
---
 src/hardware/joystick.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hardware/joystick.cpp b/src/hardware/joystick.cpp
index c88fcc35..0d6a038b 100644
--- a/src/hardware/joystick.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/joystick.cpp
@@ -260,6 +260,13 @@ void JOYSTICK_Init() {
 		button_wrapping_enabled = section->Get_bool("buttonwrap");
 		stick[0].enabled = false;
 		stick[1].enabled = false;
+#if defined(ANDROID)
+		/* Flutter supplies a synthetic stick through the bridge. Enable the
+		 * emulated ports before DOS autoexec/program startup so games that
+		 * probe the game port during initialization detect them. */
+		stick[0].enabled = (joytype != JOY_NONE);
+		stick[1].enabled = (joytype != JOY_NONE);
+#endif
 		stick[0].xtick = stick[0].ytick = stick[1].xtick =
 		                 stick[1].ytick = PIC_FullIndex();
 		
